\meta{commit}{6fad0e1}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The repository starts with a build environment that depends on nothing installed on the host. \code{\verb~|env.sh~} pins GraalVM Community Edition 25 and Maven 3.9.16 under \code{\verb~|.toolchain/~} and gives Maven a repository of its own there, so that no build touches the system JDK or a personal Maven repository; \code{\verb~|scripts/fetch-toolchain.sh~} fetches the pinned files. The parent \code{\verb~|pom.xml~} lists the modules, and each module is installed into that private repository when its own tests pass, which is what the later entries call a publication.}

\p{Detail: \src{env.sh}, \src{docs/PLATFORM.md}. Commit \commit{6fad0e1}. Session: [research, benchmark infrastructure and spikes](ses-XOS5).}
